-- title:
--   Atkin–Lehner automorphism at p ∥ M commutes with diamonds
-- statement:
--   Let $p$ be a prime and $M$ a non-zero natural number with $p \mid M$ but $p^2 \nmid M$, and let $H \le (\mathbb{Z}/M)^\times$ be a subgroup containing every unit whose image under the reduction $(\mathbb{Z}/M)^\times \to (\mathbb{Z}/(M/p))^\times$ is $1$. Write $E =$ `xHFunctionFieldBar M H` for the intermediate field of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}((q))$ over $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ generated by the image of the rational function field `xHFunctionField M H` under the coefficientwise embedding, and $E' =$ `xHFunctionFieldBar (M / p) (infSubgroup p M H hpM)` for the corresponding field at level $M/p$ and subgroup the image of $H$ under the above reduction map. Let $\theta$ be a $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$-algebra automorphism of $E$ subject to two conditions: (i) whenever $f \in E$ and $u \in E'$ have the same Laurent series, the series of $\theta f$ is $\mathrm{qExpand}\,p$ applied to that of $u$, i.e. the substitution $q \mapsto q^p$ obtained by multiplying all exponents by $p$; and (ii) for every unit $c$ of $\mathbb{Z}/(M/p)$ whose underlying residue is $p$, and all $f \in E$, $u \in E'$ with the series of $f$ equal to $\mathrm{qExpand}\,p$ of that of $u$, the series of $\theta f$ equals that of `diamondAutHBar (M / p) (infSubgroup p M H hpM) c u`. Then for every $d \in (\mathbb{Z}/M)^\times$ and every $x \in E$ one has $\theta(\langle d\rangle x) = \langle d\rangle(\theta x)$, where $\langle d\rangle =$ `diamondAutHBar M H d` is the automorphism of $E$ chosen to satisfy the predicate `IsDiamondAutHBar M H d` (acting on quotients of integral $q$-expansions of modular forms of level $\Gamma_H(M)$ by slashing with any $\gamma \in \Gamma_0(M)$ whose upper-left entry reduces to $d$ mod $M$), and equal to the identity if no such automorphism exists.
--
--   This is the field-theoretic form, over $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$, of the classical fact that the partial Atkin–Lehner involution $w_p$ at a prime exactly dividing the level normalises $\Gamma_H(M)$ and hence commutes with the diamond operators; $\theta$ plays the role of the pullback $w_p^{*}$, characterised by the two clauses relating it to the two degeneracy maps to level $M/p$. It is used in establishing the compatibility laws between the Fricke and Atkin–Lehner automorphisms and in producing generic charts for the de Rham model of $X_H$ at $p$.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_ModularCurve_algEquiv_diamondAutHBar_comm_of_qExpand_of_diamondAutHBar_div.lean

